## Focus Views

Sometimes you only want to show a specific node and its immediate neighborhood rather than a complete level view.

### Neighborhood around DB

```elixir
hops = fn i -> Choreo.View.focus(model, :db, radius: i) end

Kino.Layout.tabs(
  "1-Hop": Kino.Layout.tabs(
    Siren: Choreo.Lab.Siren.new(C4.to_mermaid(hops.(1))),
    Graphviz: Kino.VizJS.render(C4.to_dot(hops.(1))),
    Sketch: Choreo.Lab.Sketch.new(C4.to_mermaid(hops.(1)))
  ),
  "2-Hop": Kino.Layout.tabs(
    Siren: Choreo.Lab.Siren.new(C4.to_mermaid(hops.(2))),
    Graphviz: Kino.VizJS.render(C4.to_dot(hops.(2))),
    Sketch: Choreo.Lab.Sketch.new(C4.to_mermaid(hops.(2)))
  ),
  "3-Hop": Kino.Layout.tabs(
    Siren: Choreo.Lab.Siren.new(C4.to_mermaid(hops.(3))),
    Graphviz: Kino.VizJS.render(C4.to_dot(hops.(3))),
    Sketch: Choreo.Lab.Sketch.new(C4.to_mermaid(hops.(3)))
  )
)

```

### Shortest Path from Customer to Database

```elixir
path_view = Choreo.View.focus_between(model, :customer, :db)
Kino.Layout.tabs(
  Siren: Choreo.Lab.Siren.new(C4.to_mermaid(path_view)),
  Graphviz: Kino.VizJS.render(C4.to_dot(path_view)),
  Sketch: Choreo.Lab.Sketch.new(C4.to_mermaid(path_view))
)
```

